      "id": "brakes.hydraulic-race",
      "title": "Race brake hydraulic circuit (dual masters, balance bar, Bosch ABS optional)",
      "type": "hydraulic",
      "description": "Driver input through a floor-mount pedal and balance bar to separate front and rear master cylinders, each with its own reservoir. Pressure transducers tee off each circuit. The Bosch Motorsport ABS hydraulic unit sits between the masters and the corners (or is replaced by a front tee and a rear tee for an ABS-delete car). Front circuit: two hard lines through firewall bulkheads to the LF/RF hose brackets, flex hoses to 6-piston calipers. Rear circuit: one line under/inside the floor to a tee on the rear subframe, then to LR/RR flex hoses and 4-piston calipers.",
